# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COLLECTED DATA — NEVER COMMIT.
#
# Everything below contains real network-usage history from this machine:
# which executables ran, when, and how much they transferred. The repo holds
# code only. If you are adding a new collector output format, add it here
# FIRST, before you run the collector.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# the persistent SQLite database (normally on D:\, but never commit a stray copy)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# raw SRUM snapshots + ESE journals pulled via VSS
*.dat
*.jfm
*.jrs
*.chk
SRU*.log
snapshot/
snapshots/

# esentutl /p writes its integrity log to the CURRENT DIRECTORY, not beside the
# database, and appends to it forever. srum-recover.ps1 now runs repair from
# scratch so it lands there, but the collector's working directory is this
# repo, so an older build or a hand-run esentutl still drops one here.
*.INTEG.RAW

# SrumECmd CSV output
*.csv
csv-out/

# scratch space used by the collector between snapshot and ingest
temp/
tmp/

# Exported scheduled-task XML: register-task.ps1 writes it on every install, and
# it embeds that install's Windows account SID and paths -- nothing a public
# fork should carry. The working repo this was published from keeps its own two
# XMLs committed for reset recovery; they were tracked before this rule, and git
# never ignores a tracked file, so re-exports there still show as changes.
scripts/task/

# Local dev-server launch config is machine-specific tooling, not project code.
.claude/
